# Whose Agent-Feedback lines reach the agents — one identity per line.
#
# Installed by the starter kit as .agent-feedback-authors at the repository
# root, and read by scripts/feedback_tool.py (`make agent-feedback`).
#
# An identity is a commit author's email, for feedback written in commit
# messages, or a login as your code host's comment export names it, for
# feedback written in pull-request or issue comments. Case does not matter.
# Everything after '#' is a comment.
#
# A line that reaches the report can become an instruction every later agent
# session follows, so list the people whose review you would accept for a
# change to a rule. Feedback from anyone else is counted, but its text is
# left out of the report. Do not list a bot identity an agent commits as:
# that would make every agent session a trusted author.
#
# As installed, the list names nobody, and nobody's feedback is read.
#
#   maintainer@example.com
#   octocat
